            "type": "text",
            "text": "**Roster countries:** Yazaki — JPN, Sumitomo Electric — JPN, Aptiv — USA.\n\n**Same treatment:** Yazaki and Sumitomo Electric share a roster country (JPN), so on this field alone they'd group together, with Aptiv (USA) separate.\n\n**What the roster country doesn't tell you:** essentially everything that actually determines duty. It records where the supplier is based on this roster — not where the harnesses are manufactured. Wire harnesses are labor-intensive and commonly built in Mexico, North Africa, Eastern Europe, or Southeast Asia regardless of the parent company's home country. Duty depends on country of origin (including substantial-transformation rules), the tariff classification, and any trade-agreement eligibility — none of which is in this data. So I can't tell you what duty any of these three would face; I can only say two share a roster country and one doesn't."
